<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot illustrates SHAP values for ten features impacting a model, ranked by importance. Points are colored by feature value from blue \(low\) to red \(high\). Previous-injury history shows the greatest effect.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve compares three models: fusion \(solid blue line, area under the curve AUC = 0.70\), wearable-only \(green dotted line, AUC = 0.64\), and FMS-only \(red dashed line, AUC = 0.62\), with shaded regions representing confidence intervals. Fusion significantly outperforms both FMS-only \(p = 0.031\) and wearable-only \(p = 0.047\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A is a confusion matrix for injury prediction with 21 true positives, 16 false negatives, 30 false positives, and 94 true negatives. Reported metrics below include sensitivity 0.57, specificity 0.76, positive predictive value 0.46, and F1 score 0.48. Panel B is a calibration plot comparing observed injury rates to mean predicted probabilities, displaying a near-diagonal trend with error bars, base rate 23.0 percent, Brier score 0.171, and no-skill baseline 0.177.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot illustrating SHAP interaction values between ASI-PTA and ILL score, with ASI-PTA on the x-axis and SHAP interaction value on the y-axis. Data points are colored by ILL scores: red for 0, blue for 1, green for 2, and yellow-orange for 3. A blue trend line indicates a positive correlation for higher ILL scores. Mean absolute interaction SHAP value is 0.09, and stability is 71 percent of 200 resampled subsets.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
